This is the README file for the test problem distributed
with the EPS3 system. 

The directory contains a suite of data files and job
scripts to run a small test case of the EPS3 system. The
purpose is to provide templates of the job streams and 
data files as well as provide some of the default lookup
tables used by the EPS3 system.

DEFAULT INPUT FILES

The following are the default data files that can be used
for most applications of EPS3.

---------------------------------------------
inputs/chemical.speciation.xref.cb4.12Dec04
Lookup table for mapping a source category to a
speciation profile code.
Used by CHMSPL
---------------------------------------------
inputs/spatial.allocation.xref.Aug03
Lookup table for mapping a source category to a
gridded surrogate number.
Used by GRDEM
---------------------------------------------
inputs/splitfac.TOG_to_TOG.std_profiles.cb4.eps3.15jan07
inputs/splitfac.TOG_to_TOG.std_profiles.cb5.eps3.15jan07
inputs/splitfac.TOG_to_VOC.std_profiles.cb4.eps3.15jan07
inputs/splitfac.TOG_to_VOC.std_profiles.cb5.eps3.15jan07
inputs/splitfac.VOC_to_TOG.std_profiles.cb4.eps3.15jan07
inputs/splitfac.VOC_to_TOG.std_profiles.cb5.eps3.15jan07
inputs/splitfac.VOC_to_VOC.std_profiles.cb4.eps3.15jan07
inputs/splitfac.VOC_to_VOC.std_profiles.cb5.eps3.15jan07
Split factors files used to convert criteria pollutants
(VOC or TOG) to model ready species (i.e. PAR, TOL, etc.)
Used by CHMSPL
---------------------------------------------
inputs/temporal.allocation.xref_area.Aug03
inputs/temporal.allocation.xref_points.Aug03
Lookup tables for mapping a source category to a
set of temporal profiles.
Used by TMPRL
---------------------------------------------
inputs/temporal.profiles.Aug03
Data file containing the temporal profiles.
Used by TMPRL
---------------------------------------------


The following are the application specific files. These
are provided as templates.  They cannot be used for your
application.

---------------------------------------------
inputs/userin.test_problem
Global user input file (USERIN).
Used by all modules
---------------------------------------------
inputs/AFS.points.test_problem
Base inventory file for point sources.
Used by PREPNT
---------------------------------------------
inputs/AMS.area.test_problem
Base inventory file for point sources.
Used by PREAM
---------------------------------------------
inputs/LBASE_inputs.test_problem.Hays.990813
Base inventory file for link based mobile sources.
Used by LBASE.
---------------------------------------------
inputs/control.factors.area.test_problem
Sample control factors file, including examples
of all packets.
Used by CNTLEM
---------------------------------------------

JOB SCRIPTS

In ./jobs directory you will find a set of scripts
that can be utilized to run the EPS3 modules. You
may have to modify the scripts to make them work on
your system.  For example, you may have to change the
EXEC variable to match the directory structure on your
system. These scripts can also serve as templates for
building your own application.  

Here is the order you should run the scripts.

jobs/pream.area.job
jobs/prepnt.job
jobs/lbase.job
jobs/cntlem.area.job
jobs/chmspl.area.job
jobs/chmspl.points.job
jobs/tmprl.area.job
jobs/tmprl.points.job
jobs/grdem.area.job
jobs/grdem.pts.job
jobs/pstpnt.job
jobs/pigems.job
jobs/mrguam.job

The message files for this run will be found in the ./msg
directory.  For comparison purposes, we have included a
copy of the message files in the msg.distrib directory.
